%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:dctcp-accecn -- with AccECN, DcTcp counts the marked bytes from the AccECN feedback.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; the comment of
each algorithm module names its behavior. The claim of DcTcp (RFC 8257 section 3.3.3, with RFC 9768): the fraction of
marked bytes gives alpha; with AccECN the counters of the feedback give the marked bytes.

The class dctcp-accecn: DcTcp::countBytes() takes the CE bytes of the AccECN option (or the CE
packets of the ACE field times the MSS) when AccECN is negotiated, and the bytes of the ACKs
with ECE otherwise. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "dctcp" from the other algorithms, which have no
alpha.

Host under test: host1, with DcTcp and AccECN (preconditions); host2 answers AccECN
(accecn-passive). host1 sends 100000 bytes at 0.2 s, and the tap marks each data segment CE.
Observation: level 2, the first alpha, after one window of marked data, is g (0.0625).

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: dctcp-accecn
%# value: "DcTcp"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpAccEcn")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
                     .set("ipv4.ecn", "3")
                     .describe("each data segment of host1: mark it CE"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("calcLoad")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      return context.event.value >= 0.06 && context.event.value <= 0.065;
                  })
                  .describe("the first alpha, after one window of marked data")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpAccEcn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DcTcp"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn-passive"
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpAccEcn: PASS
